      "value": "What’s the point of this?\n\nA) In many countries, dial-up connections use dynamic IP addresses. Users simply get a new IP address.\n\nB) Many providers use DS-Lite connections, meaning lots of customers share the same IP address. You’d end up catching far more users than the one you actually want.\n\nC) There will certainly be quite a few users who use VRC from internet cafés or other providers. That would suddenly block all of them as well.",
